Z||000000||Jaei Sun||03-20-2001||12:34 AM||||I'm going to be changing my tranny oil from 5w30 to Redline's MTL (SAE 5w/10w30) but one thing has caught my eye in my Chilton man.  <P>It says to use SAE 85w90 which would be the Redline product Mt-90 equiv.  Now I'm confused... what type of transmission Oil does the 5-speed Getrag/Muncie Use???||||reg||5
Z||000001||862M4inCA||03-20-2001||01:11 AM||||hrm. In my Haynes manual it says to use 5W30 oil in the 5 sp. Isuzu. I just changed the oil in the transaxle before moving from CA to TX and did fine. Might be something to look into tho since I'd never heard of using motor oil in a transmission until I bought my Fiero, altho I'd heard of using ATF in a standard.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||03-20-2001||02:02 AM||||Jaei,<P>Here's a link for a thread started on the same thing:  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007352.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007352.html</A> <P>Just for future reference, on things like this that apply to almost any of our cars, there has probably been the same discussion before.  It will save everyone some time if you use the search function and search for related articles before posting a new question.  Hope this helps.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
